DAW Pro local patch 0002 against signalsmith-stretch v1.3.2 (57b93f4e9206a089a45387eaa39bdc9f310d3308) + patch 0001

Transposer peak position and flat main-lobe map (two halves; both needed).

(a) findPeaks: the peak position was an energy centroid over the region's bins,
biased toward bin centres by up to 0.076 bins (0.6 Hz at 48 kHz). On a NEW
spectrum the `rot` pass has already turned prevInput by each bin's centre
advance, so input*conj(prevInput) at bin k has phase theta*(peak - k) for a
steady partial: the patch reads the position from that phase around the
region's max bin (3 bins, all channels summed), gated by coherence
(|sum| > 0.5 * sum|terms|) and kept inside the region (+-0.5 bin), else the
centroid stands. Exact to < 1e-4 bins on steady partials.

(b) updateOutputMap: the smoothstep between a real peak and its neighbour
(a window sidelobe pseudo-peak ~53 bins away for a pure sine, or the next
harmonic) bent the offset INSIDE the peak's main lobe, so the lobe's bins
advanced at different rates (up to -12 c at -12 st). Each peak's offset is now
held flat for 0.5*N/H bins either side (upstream's smoothingBins/2; 97 % of
the analysis window's first null at presetDefault, where the lobe is -40 dB;
86 % / -21 dB at presetCheaper), capped at a quarter of BOTH the output and
the input gap, so the transition between two peaks keeps at least half of the
input bins and a non-negative energy gradient up to +12 st.

Measured (architect harness, product schedule): isolated and harmonic
partials land within 0.01 c at +-5..+-24 st, 44.1/48/96 kHz, ratios 0.5-1.5,
stereo, formant-preserve and formant shift. 0 st is byte-identical
(findPeaks/updateOutputMap run only when frequencies are mapped).
Known costs: +7 % on a transposed render; inter-harmonic noise is
redistributed toward the harmonics at large up-shifts (energy conserved);
a vibrato mean-pitch residual intrinsic to shifting a moving partial is no
longer masked. See VENDORED.md.

MUST ship with patch 0003: without it, the phase-derived position is taken
over an H+-1-sample interval but divided by the H turn, and near-unity ratios
regress (17/104 measured rows worse than 0001 alone).

Apply (from Sources/CSignalsmithStretch), after 0001:
    patch -p1 < patches/0002-peak-position-and-flat-lobe-map.patch

